# {Workspace Name}

{One sentence: what this workspace does and what leaves it.}

This workspace uses ICM: numbering carries sequence, hierarchy scopes context, and files carry state.

## Where things live

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `CONTEXT.md` | Route map and pipeline status contract |
| `stages/` | Ordered stage contracts and per-run outputs |
| `_shared/` | Stable rules used across runs |
| `_templates/` | Blank starters for repeatable artifacts |
| `setup/` | One-time factory configuration |

## Route

| Request | Start at |
|---|---|
| New run | `stages/01-{name}/CONTEXT.md` |
| Resume reviewed run | The next stage named in `CONTEXT.md` |
| Status | Scan the declared output or receipt locations |
| Setup | `setup/questionnaire.md` |

## Boundary

Nothing moves downstream until the previous artifact passes its Human Check. Do not load the whole workspace when a stage contract names a smaller context set.
